.he "fd2 (1)                      8/19/26                      fd2 (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
fd2
- redirect file descriptor 2 (diagnostic output)
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
fd2
[ fd2arg ] command [ command-arg ] ...
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
.it Fd2
executes
.it command
with file descriptor 2 (the diagnostic output) redirected to a file
or to the standard output.  There are three forms:
.sp
.in +5
fd2 \-file comd ...	[write on
.it file
]
.br
fd2 \-\-file comd ...	[append to
.it file
]
.br
fd2 + comd ...	[causes file descriptor 2 to be made the same as
file descriptor 1]
.in -5
.sp
In either of the first two cases, omission of
.it file
causes
.bd msg.out
to be used as the output file.  Omission of
.it fd2arg
has the effect of
.bd \-msg.out.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
sh (1), msh (1)
